exam: It is given that {a} acquires {p} packs of {q} {t} together with {r} packs of {s} {t}, and subsequently transfers {g} {t} to {b}. Determine the aggregate quantity of {t} remaining in the possession of {a}.
exam: Whereas a retail establishment holds {p} boxes of {q} pens and {r} boxes of {s} pens, and {g} pens are thereafter sold, ascertain the number of pens remaining in stock.
exam: Shells were collected at the rate of {q} per day for a period of {p} days and at the rate of {s} per day for a further {r} days; {g} of the shells so collected were found to be broken. State the number of unbroken shells.
exam: Compute the total quantity of {t} remaining, given {p} packs containing {q} {t} each, {r} packs containing {s} {t} each, and the subsequent removal of {g} {t}.
exercise: When Grandma passed away, {a} got her sewing things: {p} tins of {q} buttons and {r} jars of {s} buttons. {a.He} gave {g} buttons to {b}. How many buttons does {a} have now?
exercise: Business was "challenging", so the shop sold things off cheap. It had {p} boxes of {q} pens and {r} boxes of {s} pens, and it sold {g} pens. How many pens are left?
test: my "little darling" of a brother binned {g} of my {t}, the pest. had {p} packs of {q} and {r} packs of {s}. how many i got now
